# Getter and Setter

By default, computed properties are **read-only**. But you can provide a setter to make them writable.

```javascript
computed: {
  fullName: {
    get() {
      return this.firstName + ' ' + this.lastName;
    },
    set(newValue) {
      const names = newValue.split(' ');
      this.firstName = names[0];
      this.lastName = names[names.length - 1];
    }
  }
}
```

Now you can use `v-model` on `fullName` or assign a value directly.
